# What an editor's clangd is told about this tree. README.md, *Testing*, is how the compilation
# database it reads alongside this gets written.

# clangd runs its own include cleaner, which is not the clang-tidy check of the same name that
# .clang-tidy already turns off. Both are off for the same reason: this tree includes what a file
# reads rather than what the compiler can prove it needs, and the suggestion fires on every
# header that exists to be re-exported.
Diagnostics:
  UnusedIncludes: None
  MissingIncludes: None

---
# The files in fb2k_unparsed_sources (scripts/lib/compile-flags.sh), which the pattern below
# repeats, have no entry in the compilation database, because this Mac's clang cannot parse them.
# So clangd guesses the flags from a sibling, the first missing header is a file-not-found, and
# every diagnostic after it is cascade from that. None of them is about the code.
# CONTRIBUTING.md's section 1, rule 4, is what does govern these files: they are reviewed here
# and compiled for the first time by scripts/build.ps1. The rest of src/fb2k/ has database
# entries once scripts/fetch-sdk.sh has fetched the SDK, and shows its diagnostics; without
# the SDK, every file there shows the cascade.
If:
  PathMatch: src/fb2k/(preferences|aac_encoder|browser|ui_assets)\.cpp
# Suppress does not reach the fatal clang emits when it gives up counting, so the count is
# lifted instead and nothing is left to give up over.
CompileFlags:
  Add: [-ferror-limit=0]
Diagnostics:
  Suppress: '*'
